.TH LIBMPQ__UPDATE_BEGIN_MPQE 3 2026-09-29 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__update_begin_mpqe \- begin an authenticated MPQE update transaction
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.B "int32_t libmpq__update_begin_mpqe("
.B "        mpq_update_s **update, const char *archive_path,"
.B "        const uint8_t *auth_code, size_t auth_code_size"
.B ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens an existing filesystem MPQE archive with the explicit caller-supplied authentication code. At least 32 bytes are required. The code is borrowed only during this call; libmpq keeps the minimal private authentication data needed to re-encrypt on commit and clears it when the transaction is consumed.
.PP
The decoded MPQ is staged in a same-directory, owner-only plaintext temporary file. Replace, remove, and rename use the ordinary update operations. Commit re-encrypts the working archive into a private sibling, verifies that it opens with the supplied code, and atomically replaces the original. Abort discards staged data. Both operations consume the handle even on error. A no-op commit leaves the MPQE file byte-identical. Modifications remove stale weak signatures; no external strong-signature representation is defined for MPQE transport.
.PP
The original remains unchanged on handled pre-publication failures. Cleanup is best effort: an abnormal process or system termination can leave plaintext temporary data behind. The destination identity is rechecked immediately before publication on a best-effort basis; this is not a lock or conditional replacement.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns \fBLIBMPQ_SUCCESS\fP on success, or a negative libmpq error. On failure, \fI*update\fP is NULL.
.SH ERRORS
Missing or short authentication data returns \fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_DECRYPT\fP. Wrong credentials, invalid archives, allocation, and backing I/O failures return existing negative libmpq errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq__update_begin (3),
.BR libmpq__update_commit (3),
.BR libmpq__update_abort (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_open_mpqe (3)
